* Checks that activities scheduled for year 0 (every cycle) share one copy
* of their parameters across cycles instead of duplicating the parameters and
* potentially overwhelming the maximum number of parameters per simulation
* (base/opexpn.f). Run with: make  (acb01 = normal run, acb02 = stop/restart)
*
* Stands 1 vs 2 and 3 vs 4 compare a stand with many year-0 activities
* against a control without them. FVS copies year-0 activities into each
* cycle with separate code depending on whether the stand also has dated
* activities, so both cases are tested:
*   Stand 1: 50 FIXMORT and 50 FIXDG rows at year 0, each with a multiplier
*            of 1.0 so they do not change growth or mortality, plus a
*            year-0 COMPUTE. No dated activities.
*   Stand 2: control for stand 1. The year-0 COMPUTE only.
*   Stand 3: the same as stand 1 plus a dated THINBTA in 2040.
*   Stand 4: control for stand 3. The year-0 COMPUTE and the THINBTA only.
* Duplicating the parameters of the FIXMORT and FIXDG rows for every cycle
* would need about 10,000 parameter slots (the limit is 7,999), so FVS would
* stop early with an FVS10 error. With the change to reuse the initial set of
* parameters in all cycles, all 20 cycles run and the summaries of stands 1
* and 3 match their controls.
*
* COMPUTE still keeps its own parameters for each cycle, because it stores
* each cycle's result in them. Stands 1-4 compute XBBA (stand basal area),
* and the activity summary in the .out file lists the value for each cycle
* ("CMPU XBBA ... DONE IN"). The values should change from cycle to cycle
* and match between stands 1 and 2 and between stands 3 and 4. If COMPUTE
* shared its parameters, every cycle would show the last cycle's value.
*
* Stands 5 vs 6 check that a shared multiplier still applies in every cycle:
*   Stand 5: one FIXDG 1.2 at year 0.
*   Stand 6: the same FIXDG 1.2, dated in each of the 20 cycles.
* Their summaries must match.
*
* acb01 and acb02 diff allcycle_budget.sum against allcycle_budget.sum.save
* and the XBBA lines against allcycle_budget.xbba.save. Both saved files were
* checked against the comparisons above when they were saved.
SCREEN
STATS
TREEFMT
(T24,I4,T1,I4,T31,F2.0,I1,A3,F3.1,F2.1,T45,F3.0,T63,F3.0,T60,F3.1,T48,I1,
T52,I2,T66,5I1,T54,7I1,T75,F3.0)

